// Test: bugfixes/codegen_string_arg_alias_jsonget_plugin_narrows_params
// Regression for CODEGEN-STRING-ARG-ALIAS-JSONGET (fingerprint 3957fce4).
//
// frame.server's plugin.toml declared `_json_get` with
// `params = ["string", "string"]`, which overwrote the compiler's builtin
// `json.get(any, string) -> any` symbol at resolver-registration time.
// The narrower param list disabled the MIR builder's auto-boxing at the
// call site (see `needs_boxing` in mir_builder/expressions.rs), so a String
// argument flowed into json.get's WASM code without being wrapped in a
// boxed Any struct. The stdlib json.get code reads offset 0 as the Any
// type tag, but a raw Clean string's offset 0 is the length prefix — the
// mis-branch produced a garbage inner pointer and the subsequent
// json.textToData call read out-of-bounds memory (crash surfaced as
// `String read out of bounds: ptr=NNNNN, len=1400000000+`).
//
// Fix: `register_language_function_aliases` now skips plugin aliases whose
// parameter list would narrow a builtin `Any` param to a specific type.
// The runtime contract (json.get expects a boxed Any first arg) is
// preserved regardless of what the plugin declares in its plugin.toml.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.44
//
// Expected output:
//   Alice

start:
	string j = "{\"name\":\"Alice\",\"age\":30}"
	string got = json.get(j, "name")
	print(got) +
